\name{cellucid_cells_visibility_set}
\alias{cellucid_cells_visibility_set}
\title{Hide or show cells}
\usage{
cellucid_cells_visibility_set(viewer, cells, visible)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{cells}{Either cells: 1-based positions, \code{TRUE}/\code{FALSE} for every cell, or the cell names of the object the viewer shows, each once (sent as original positions); or \code{NULL} (Every cell). Required.}
\item{visible}{true to show them, false to hide them. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Hide or show cells one by one in the selected view, on top of every filter.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{cells.visibility.set} (Cells). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{visibility}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_cells_visibility_set(viewer, cells = c(0,
      1, 2), visible = FALSE)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
